hints:
Use only `<` so strings and doubles work too. `max_of` is `*std::max_element(v.begin(), v.end())`; `min_max` is `std::minmax_element`, which returns a pair of iterators:
```cpp
auto [lo, hi] = std::minmax_element(v.begin(), v.end());
return {*lo, *hi};
```

Loops and locals are allowed in C++14+ `constexpr` functions; the starter only lacks the keyword and the loop:
```cpp
constexpr long long ipow(long long base, int exp) {
    long long r = 1;
    while (exp-- > 0) r *= base;
    return r;
}
```
